Agreed; I think I suggested that in another post.

> Also, any hit that does less than (say) 4 damage should not split the
> pudding -- no more poking at it with rusty -3 scalpels.

I don't see why not, if, for example, splitting the pudding results in two
puddings each with 50% (or whatever) of the max HP of the original.  I like
50%, because it keeps the total max HP constant.  Then if you make the
minimum possible max HP after the split minhp, and the initial max HP is
maxhp, the total number of puddings you could create is maxhp/minhp.

If this were combined with not effectively generating new items at each
split, the behaviour would seem more intuitive, which I think is a good
thing in this case.

